<DocsLayout title="Advanced LangChain guide | dotfetch" description="Approval, run context, tracing and error modes for dotfetch's LangChain tools.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Advanced framework guide</p>
  <h1>Advanced LangChain</h1>
  <p class="lead">Approval, run context and tracing for dotfetch's LangChain tools. Per-turn selection is covered in the LangGraph guide, since <code>create_agent</code> runs on LangGraph.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/dotfetch/docs/frameworks/langchain/">← Basic LangChain usage</a></p>

  <h2>Human approval</h2>
  <p>A confirmation-gated tool (<code>requires_confirmation=True</code> or a <code>SecurityPolicy</code> pattern) pauses a LangGraph-backed run, which includes every <code>create_agent</code> agent, with <code>interrupt()</code>. Resume with <code>Command(resume=True)</code> to run it once. The run needs a checkpointer. Outside a graph, for example when you call <code>model.bind_tools(tools)</code> and invoke tools yourself, the model is told the call needs approval and it is not run. See <a href="/dotfetch/docs/frameworks/langgraph/advanced/">Advanced LangGraph</a> for the full flow.</p>

  <h2>Run context</h2>
  <p><code>current_tool_runtime()</code> returns the run a dotfetch tool is executing in: <code>.config</code> (the <code>RunnableConfig</code>), <code>.tool_call_id</code>, and inside LangGraph <code>.context</code> and <code>.store</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from dotfetch.langchain import current_tool_runtime

@fetcher.register
def audit_note(text: str) -> str:
    """Attach a note to the current conversation's audit log."""
    runtime = current_tool_runtime()
    thread = (runtime.config or {}).get("configurable", {}).get("thread_id")
    return audit.write(thread, runtime.tool_call_id, text)`} />

  <h2>Tracing</h2>
  <p>An active OpenTelemetry span, or else the current LangSmith run, becomes the dotfetch <code>ToolCall</code>'s <code>trace_id</code> and <code>parent_span_id</code>.</p>

  <h2>Error modes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>error_mode="model"</code> (default): failures become error <code>ToolMessage</code>s; gated calls interrupt for approval.</li>
    <li><code>error_mode="raise"</code>: <code>ToolExecutionError</code> (and <code>ToolConfirmationRequiredError</code> for gated calls) propagates; no interrupt.</li>
    <li><code>error_formatter=fn</code>: rewrites the failure text; if it raises, the model gets a generic message instead.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
